#: tutorials/3d/csg_tools.rst:244
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Rebel Engine's :doc:`spatial_material` supports *triplanar mapping*, which "
"can be used to automatically apply a texture to arbitrary objects without "
"distortion. This is handy when using CSG as Rebel Engine doesn't support "
"editing UV maps on CSG nodes yet. Triplanar mapping is relatively slow, "
"which usually restricts its usage to organic surfaces like terrain. Still, "
"when prototyping, it can be used to quickly apply textures to CSG-based "
"levels."
msgstr ""
