"records) of key-value pairs. When one attempts to access a value, they "
"provide it a key. It then *hashes* the key, i.e. converts it into a number. "
"The \"hash\" is used to calculate the index into the array. As an array, the "
"OHM then has a quick lookup within the \"table\" of keys mapped to values. "
"When the HashMap becomes too full, it increases to the next power of 2 (so, "
"16 records, then 32, etc.) and rebuilds the structure."
msgstr ""
