"Every Rebel Project has an inherent default theme that contains the settings "
"used by the built-in control nodes. This is what gives the controls their "
"distinct look out of the box. A theme only describes the configuration, "
"however, and it is still the job of each individual control to use that "
"configuration in the way it requires to display itself. This is important to "
"remember when implementing :doc:`your own custom controls </tutorials/ui/"
"custom_gui_controls>`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/ui/gui_skinning.rst:40
msgid ""
"Even the Rebel Editor itself relies on the default theme. But it doesn't "
"look the same as a Rebel Project, because it applies its own heavily "
"customized theme on top of the default one. In principle, this works exactly "
"like it would in your game as explained :ref:`below <tutorials/ui/"
"gui_skinning:customizing a project>`."
